--  POSIX's error numbers as atoms, one for every errno Linux, Darwin and
--  FreeBSD define, named after the C macro in lower case, with each
--  system's number kept.  The names and numbers were read from Linux 7.1's
--  include/uapi/asm-generic/errno-base.h and errno.h, which x86-64, arm64
--  and RV64 share, from FreeBSD 15's sys/errno.h, the same on both of its
--  architectures, and from the macOS SDK's sys/errno.h; the C peer of
--  abi/posix-errno-numbers holds every entry to each system's own header.
--  An alias names no atom of its own: EWOULDBLOCK is EAGAIN's number on
--  all three and is `eagain`, Linux's EDEADLOCK is `edeadlk`, and
--  ENOTSUP, a number of its own only on Darwin, is EOPNOTSUPP's on Linux
--  and FreeBSD, where a failure gives `eopnotsupp`.

--- A failure no errno this module names describes: a number newer than
--- its tables, or a record the system filled that could not be read.  Its
--- `number` is zero.
public unlisted: atom

--- errno EPERM: Operation not permitted.
public eperm: atom
--- errno ENOENT: No such file or directory.
public enoent: atom
--- errno ESRCH: No such process.
public esrch: atom
--- errno EINTR: Interrupted system call.
public eintr: atom
--- errno EIO: I/O error.
public eio: atom
--- errno ENXIO: No such device or address.
public enxio: atom
--- errno E2BIG: Argument list too long.
public e2big: atom
--- errno ENOEXEC: Exec format error.
public enoexec: atom
--- errno EBADF: Bad file number.
public ebadf: atom
--- errno ECHILD: No child processes.
public echild: atom
--- errno EAGAIN: Try again.
public eagain: atom
--- errno ENOMEM: Out of memory.
public enomem: atom
--- errno EACCES: Permission denied.
public eacces: atom
--- errno EFAULT: Bad address.
public efault: atom
--- errno ENOTBLK: Block device required.
public enotblk: atom
--- errno EBUSY: Device or resource busy.
public ebusy: atom
--- errno EEXIST: File exists.
public eexist: atom
--- errno EXDEV: Cross-device link.
public exdev: atom
--- errno ENODEV: No such device.
public enodev: atom
--- errno ENOTDIR: Not a directory.
public enotdir: atom
--- errno EISDIR: Is a directory.
public eisdir: atom
--- errno EINVAL: Invalid argument.
public einval: atom
--- errno ENFILE: File table overflow.
public enfile: atom
--- errno EMFILE: Too many open files.
public emfile: atom
--- errno ENOTTY: Not a typewriter.
public enotty: atom
--- errno ETXTBSY: Text file busy.
public etxtbsy: atom
--- errno EFBIG: File too large.
public efbig: atom
--- errno ENOSPC: No space left on device.
public enospc: atom
--- errno ESPIPE: Illegal seek.
public espipe: atom
--- errno EROFS: Read-only file system.
public erofs: atom
--- errno EMLINK: Too many links.
public emlink: atom
--- errno EPIPE: Broken pipe.
public epipe: atom
--- errno EDOM: Math argument out of domain of func.
public edom: atom
--- errno ERANGE: Math result not representable.
public erange: atom
--- errno EDEADLK: Resource deadlock would occur.
public edeadlk: atom
--- errno ENAMETOOLONG: File name too long.
public enametoolong: atom
--- errno ENOLCK: No record locks available.
public enolck: atom
--- errno ENOSYS: Invalid system call number.
public enosys: atom
--- errno ENOTEMPTY: Directory not empty.
public enotempty: atom
--- errno ELOOP: Too many symbolic links encountered.
public eloop: atom
--- errno ENOMSG: No message of desired type.
public enomsg: atom
--- errno EIDRM: Identifier removed.
public eidrm: atom
--- errno ECHRNG: Channel number out of range.
public echrng: atom
--- errno EL2NSYNC: Level 2 not synchronized.
public el2nsync: atom
--- errno EL3HLT: Level 3 halted.
public el3hlt: atom
--- errno EL3RST: Level 3 reset.
public el3rst: atom
--- errno ELNRNG: Link number out of range.
public elnrng: atom
--- errno EUNATCH: Protocol driver not attached.
public eunatch: atom
--- errno ENOCSI: No CSI structure available.
public enocsi: atom
--- errno EL2HLT: Level 2 halted.
public el2hlt: atom
--- errno EBADE: Invalid exchange.
public ebade: atom
--- errno EBADR: Invalid request descriptor.
public ebadr: atom
--- errno EXFULL: Exchange full.
public exfull: atom
--- errno ENOANO: No anode.
public enoano: atom
